{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.double_braiding_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.double_braiding_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.lean#L75-L100","doc":"**The gate.** An element satisfying the Hecke relation has trivial double\nbraiding exactly when `q² = 1`.\n\nThe forward direction is the one that matters for the eightfold surface: if the\nbraiding were symmetric, the substrate parameter would be forced onto `q² = 1`.\nThe reverse direction is what makes this an honest `iff` rather than a bound —\nat `q² = 1` the Hecke relation really does degenerate to `σ² = 1`, so the\nstatement is not vacuously one-sided. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.hecke_rel_iff_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.hecke_rel_iff_factored","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric.lean#L58-L73","doc":"The Hecke relation in its two standard spellings. The factored form\n`(σ - q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0` exhibits the eigenvalues; the quadratic form\n`σ² = (q - q⁻¹)σ + 1` is what the braid relation is usually reduced against.\nThey agree precisely because `q · q⁻¹ = 1`, which is where `hq` is spent. ","signatureChunk":0}]}